id: punisher-guard
name: Punisher Guard
uaType: technical
prerequisite: Personality Score of 8+
tpCost: 15
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerBaseTier: 3
requiresTarget: true
# "Target an Opponent who is not at Long Range" - refused before it is paid - "Trigger the Exploit Maneuver of that
# Opponent": offered to them on its card. Taken: their attack held, and a Basic Attack out of sequence at them offered to
# you; through a Health Threshold or Defeated by it, their attack cancelled, its Ki back. Not taken: the card's Not
# taken button, 1d10(bT) Life and Ki Points (chat.mjs postPunisherGuard).
punisherGuard: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  An Opponent not at Long Range may Exploit you: if they do, a Basic Attack at them out of sequence - through a Health
  Threshold or Defeated, their attack is cancelled; if they do not, regain 1d10(bT) Life and Ki Points.
text: >
  Punisher Guard: Complete ego, you’re showing it off, and any reasonable person would want to knock you down a peg, to
  smack that smug grin off your face, leaving them wide open.
  –Ability Type: Technical
  –Prerequisites: Personality Score of 8+
  –TP Cost: 15
  –KP Cost: 3(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent who is not at Long Range. Trigger the Exploit Maneuver of that Opponent. If that Opponent
  uses the Exploit Maneuver in response to this effect, you may use the Basic Attack Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence
  Maneuver targeting that Opponent. If this Attacking Maneuver knocks that Opponent through a Health Threshold or Defeats
  them, their Attacking Maneuver is canceled (they regain any Ki Points spent on that Maneuver, but do not regain their
  Counter Action).

  If your targeted Opponent does not use the Exploit Maneuver in response to this effect, regain 1d10(bT) Life and Ki
  Points.
